  (text "Commander tray carrier (rev R0) - the strip under the sliding tray's two module bays.  It takes two Framework Laptop 16\nB-size input modules (numpad, RGB macropad, or any module built to github.com/FrameworkComputer/InputModules) on\nspring (pogo) contacts, and holds them with magnets.  Upstream: one USB 2.0 port on a USB-C receptacle at the tray's\ninner end (in the Commander: the hub board's free USB2517 port 7; on its own: any computer).\nA WCH CH334P hub gives each module its own downstream port; each bay's 5 V and 3.3 V are switched on only while a\nmodule sits in it (see 02_tr_ports.net)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.524 1.524)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c81780e4-4fcf-5bed-8193-00bb65bb2757"))
